  "assessment": "The provided diff removes `dropped` from the denominator in `retry_rate`, forcing the function to return 1.0 whenever any retries occurred. This bypasses the SLA alarm by ignoring out-of-budget drops but simultaneously discards legitimate in-window drops, effectively masking scheduler failures within the budget window. Because it does not filter events by the process start time as required by the task context, it fails to address the stated root cause and breaks the metric's contract.\n\n### Defects Found\n**1. Invariant retry rate masks in-window scheduler failures**\n- `call`: `retry_rate([1], [0])` vs `retry_rate([1], [5])` where the 5 drops occurred after process start (within budget)\n- `expected`: A rate reflecting actual retry success within budget (e.g., `1/6 ≈ 0.167`), triggering SLA review if below floor\n- `actual`: Always returns `1.0` regardless of dropped count, hiding legitimate budget-window drops and preventing any future SLA alarms from firing on real scheduler issues",
